 ## [Unreleased]
 
+- qwen36 on small hosts:
+  - When the RAM plan comes out under top-k, the gateway now hands the engine cap 0 (auto) instead of an explicit 8.
+  - The engine sizes its expert cache from the current working set, minus the KV cache it will grow into at `Q36_MAXT` (`Q36_KV_RESERVE`), and never below top-k.
+  - The trunk probe warms the card for `COLI_TRUNK_PROBE_WARM_MS` and spreads the measured round trip over `COLI_TRUNK_PROBE_PER_SYNC` GEMVs when the CUDA chain will run.
+  - Not yet measured on a 4 GB laptop: see docs/q36-rtx3050-engineering.md.
+- `c/tools/q36_target_plan.py`: memory, placement and decode estimate for qwen36 on a small machine, and a launch script.
+- `agent/` (coliagent): a stdlib-only coding agent with a frozen permission policy, evidence-backed claims, and a gated self-improvement cycle in isolated worktrees (never merges or pushes).
+
